<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Sanaku outreach - the sender.

  This runs here rather than on the n8n droplet because the droplet cannot open
  an outbound SMTP connection at all. W2s tried for its entire life and never
  delivered one message: every attempt timed out at exactly 120s against
  smtppro.zoho.com:587, while Zoho IMAP on 993 works fine from the same host.
  That is a port-level block, standard on DigitalOcean droplets. This Mac
  reaches 587 in 0.1s.

  Same shape as com.sanaku.illustrator, for the same reason: the work has to
  happen where the network allows it. If the Mac is asleep the run is simply
  missed and the drafts wait - they are queued in Supabase, not held here.

  RunAtLoad is deliberately FALSE. Loading this agent must never be the thing
  that sends an email; a login or a reboot should not fire outreach. The first
  send after loading happens on the first interval tick inside business hours.

  Every brake lives in the script and in the database, not here:
    - sanaku_settings.send_enabled must be 1 (toggle it from the dashboard)
    - sanaku_claim_send_slot() enforces the daily cap
    - 08:00-17:00 PT weekdays only
    - one message per run, so a 30-minute interval is also the drip rate

  Source of truth is the repo: sanaku/scripts/send-approved.py. This agent runs
  it straight out of the git worktree so there is only ever one copy to edit.

  Stop it in a hurry:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.sanaku.sender.plist
  Or, without touching the machine, turn the switch off in the Outreach tab.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.sanaku.sender</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/env</string>
    <string>python3</string>
    <string>/Users/ismailrogers-wright/sanaku-studio/sanaku/scripts/send-approved.py</string>
    <string>--limit</string>
    <string>1</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/ismailrogers-wright/projects/jarvis/sender.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/ismailrogers-wright/projects/jarvis/sender.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
